---
description: Route feature work through the top-level full-stack instruction file before narrowing into backend or frontend execution
globs:
  - backend/**
  - frontend/**
  - readme.md
alwaysApply: true
---

Use the full-stack parent instructions first whenever a request may involve product behavior, feature development, API contracts, UI integration, or architecture decisions.

Route the task into one of three paths:

- backend-only
- frontend-only
- coordinated full-stack work

For feature requests:

- ask 3 important clarification questions when the request is ambiguous
- confirm the user flow plus API inputs and outputs
- draft a zoomed-out Mermaid architecture diagram of the full backend/frontend flow before implementing meaningful changes
- add a focused Mermaid diagram for the particular backend or frontend slice being modified when the task is non-trivial
- treat the repository as a practical task platform by default, not a showcase scaffold
- bias toward deterministic product workflows, typed task contracts, and reliability behavior over explanatory demo surfaces
- reuse existing backend modules and frontend patterns when relevant
- do backend contract work before frontend integration when both stacks change
- verify both stacks before finishing

Read and follow:

@.cursor/fullstack-agentic-flow.md
